# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Finding: RBP-F001-X3
# Title:   SHUTDOWN_FINALIZER_THREADS static Mutex lacks rationale comment
# Triaged: 2026-05-14T00:00:00Z
# Mode:    initial_pass
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Sweep result: The rationale comment already exists on ALL branches.
# Lines 48-51 of runtime_health.rs contain: "Timed-out shutdown workers are
# retained in one process-wide registry instead of being dropped orphaned;
# this must be static because the bounded finalizer helper can outlive any one
# dispatcher instance after timeout, while orderly shutdown and serial tests
# still need one place to recover and join those retained workers later."
# The comment also addresses Send+Sync safety (Mutex<Vec<JoinHandle<()>>> is
# Send+Sync by Rust stdlib guarantees; no unsafe involved).
# Finding is ABSENT on all branches — the QA finding was stale at triage time.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

